    fix(harness, CF-277): validate CF_RUN_ID and confine the codex turn home to a mktemp dir
    
    The --turn branch of the codex adapter built the isolated CODEX_HOME out of an
    unvalidated CF_RUN_ID and then deleted that path twice: once before creating it
    and once from the EXIT trap. A value such as ../../victim makes the joined path
    escape the cache root, so the recursive delete and the trap both land on an
    unrelated directory — reproduced on a copy carrying only the CF-278 spelling fix,
    where $HOME/victim and its sentinel were removed.
    
    Two changes, both fail-closed:
    
      * Admission. validate_vars() now refuses CF_RUN_ID unless it is a bare
        identifier (^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$, at most 128 characters) via
        `refuse run_id`, exit 2, quoting the refused value truncated to 64 chars.
        Slashes, a dot-dot segment, a leading dot, whitespace, '$', ';' and an
        over-long id are all refused before anything is created or removed.
        CF_RUN_ID stays in REQUIRED and the contract:CF_RUN_ID record line is
        unchanged.
    
      * Containment. The turn home is now a fresh `mktemp -d` leaf under
        ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/cf-codex (created mode 700, umask 077) and
        is never derived from CF_RUN_ID. A new inside_turn_cache helper case-matches
        the path against the cache root: the EXIT trap removes the directory only
        when it answers yes and reports nothing when it answers no. The pre-create
        delete is gone — a fresh mktemp needs none. argv, timeout, sandbox, the
        auth.json copy, model_served parsing and the report shape are untouched, and
        --check / --apply keep their exit codes.
    
    Fixture, tests/harness/codex-install-test.sh section D (hermetic, fresh $FAKEHOME,
    stub codex, no network):
    
      PASS  D1a --check refuses CF_RUN_ID='../../victim' — refused and named the reason
      PASS  D1a the refusal quotes the value it refused
      PASS  D1a $SB/victim and its file survive the refusal
      PASS  D1a the traversal target under $HOME also survives the refusal
      PASS  D1b --turn refuses the same id (the mode that reaches the delete) — refused and named the reason
      PASS  D1b neither sentinel was removed in --turn
      PASS  D1b a refused run created nothing under $HOME/.cache
      PASS  D1c refused run_id=../victim (9 chars) ... refused run_id=aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa (129 chars)
      PASS  D2 --run-id r-lane is admitted (rc=0; verdict: CODEX: PASS)
      PASS  D2 the CF_RUN_ID contract record line is still emitted
      PASS  D3 the stub codex was really invoked (FAIL turn_exit row present)
      PASS  D3a the reported turn_home is a mktemp directory under the cache root: .../home-turn/.cache/cf-codex/run.b5lrr45x
      PASS  D3a the turn home carries no part of the run id
      PASS  D3b that exact directory is gone after the run
      PASS  D3c the sentinel beside the turn home still exists (the trap removed only its own leaf)
    
    The fixture goes RED on the old tree, both ways: against HEAD's installer it ends
    "codex installer test: 35 passed, 12 failed, 1 skipped / RESULT: FAIL", and against
    a copy carrying only the ${VAR[CF_RUN_ID]} spelling fix (CF-278 patched, CF-277
    absent) it ends "33 passed, 14 failed" with
    "FAIL  D1b a refused --turn removed a sentinel" and
    "FAIL  D3a the turn home is still derived from CF_RUN_ID: .../cf-codex/r-lane".
    
    Measured gates at this tree: `bash -n` clean on both scripts; the installer
    battery `codex installer test: 47 passed, 0 failed, 1 skipped / RESULT: PASS`;
    `bash tests/selftest.sh` -> `SELFTEST: PASS` (rc 0, 51 s, 351 PASS rows, the 58
    deliberate red-proof `FAIL` rows included as at base); `master_doc_check.py
    docs/master --only 16-` -> MASTER-DOC: PASS. Live legs, the full suite and the
    judge were left to the foreman, per the brief.
    
    The broken `$VAR[CF_RUN_ID]` expansion reported as CF-278 is removed by this
    change (the value is no longer joined into a path at all); the board owns that
    row and it is not closed here.
    
    docs/master/16-scripts-harness-install-codex-sh.md gains one sentence recording
    that the run id is validated and the turn home is a mktemp directory.
    
